# Build context exclusions.
#
# The first entry is the one that matters. `.env` holds the OpenRouter, Groq and
# GitHub credentials, and AGENTS.md forbids credentials reaching prompts, traces,
# indexed content or deliverables - an image layer is all four at once, and a
# layer cannot be un-published once pushed. Secrets reach the container at RUN
# time through `env_file`, never at BUILD time.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Credentials and local state that must never be baked in
.venv/
venv/
*.pem
*.key

# Generated at run time and mounted as volumes instead, so a stale copy cannot be
# shipped inside the image and then silently shadowed - or worse, NOT shadowed,
# leaving the container serving an index whose freshness manifest describes a
# different machine's last sync (F-15.2).
data/index/
data/generated/
data/feedback/

# History and tooling: large, and irrelevant to running the product
.git/
.github/
.claude/
docs/chat-history-raw.jsonl
notebooks/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
